# EKS Elastic Stack with ECK, GP3 EBS, and AWS ALB

This guide deploys an Elastic Stack on Amazon EKS using the Elastic Cloud on Kubernetes (ECK) operator.

## Architecture

```text
                         Internet
                            |
                            | HTTPS :443
                            v
                  +---------------------+
                  |  Internet-facing ALB |
                  +----------+----------+
                             |
                             | HTTPS :5601
                             v
                  +---------------------+
                  |   Kibana Service    |
                  +----------+----------+
                             |
                             v
                       Kibana Pod
                             |
                             |
                    ECK-managed cluster
                             |
              +--------------+--------------+
              |              |              |
              v              v              v
        Elasticsearch  Elasticsearch  Elasticsearch
             -0             -1             -2
              |              |              |
              v              v              v
           PVC/GP3        PVC/GP3        PVC/GP3
              |              |              |
              +--------------+--------------+
                             |
                         AWS EBS GP3
```

---

# 1. Prerequisites

You need:

* AWS account
* Existing EKS cluster
* AWS CLI
* `kubectl`
* Helm
* IAM permissions to manage EKS/IAM/EC2/ELB resources
* EBS CSI driver
* AWS Load Balancer Controller
* ECK Operator

Check the tools:

```bash
aws --version
kubectl version --client
helm version
```

---

# 2. Configure AWS CLI

Check the current identity:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

Set your cluster details:

```bash
export CLUSTER_NAME=<your-cluster-name>
export AWS_REGION=<your-region>
```

Example:

```bash
export CLUSTER_NAME=eks-demo
export AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-2
```

