# 3. Configure kubectl for EKS

Run:

```bash
aws eks update-kubeconfig \
  --region "$AWS_REGION" \
  --name "$CLUSTER_NAME"
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Expected:

```text
NAME                                         STATUS   ROLES
ip-10-xxx-xxx-xxx.ap-southeast-2.compute... Ready    <none>
ip-10-xxx-xxx-xxx.ap-southeast-2.compute... Ready    <none>
```

