# 4. Install / verify EBS CSI Driver

The EBS CSI driver is required for Elasticsearch persistent storage using EBS.

Check:

```bash
aws eks describe-addon \
  --cluster-name "$CLUSTER_NAME" \
  --addon-name aws-ebs-csi-driver \
  --region "$AWS_REGION"
```

If it is not installed:

```bash
aws eks create-addon \
  --cluster-name "$CLUSTER_NAME" \
  --addon-name aws-ebs-csi-driver \
  --region "$AWS_REGION"
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep ebs-csi
```

You should see controller and node pods.

---

# 5. Create GP3 StorageClass

We do not want Elasticsearch to use the old `gp2` StorageClass.

Create:

```bash
vi gp3-storageclass.yaml
```

Contents:

```yaml
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass

metadata:
  name: gp3
  annotations:
    storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class: "true"

provisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com

volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer

allowVolumeExpansion: true

parameters:
  type: gp3
  encrypted: "true"
  fsType: ext4
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply -f gp3-storageclass.yaml
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get storageclass
```

Expected:

```text
NAME            PROVISIONER             RECLAIMPOLICY
gp3 (default)   ebs.csi.aws.com         Delete
gp2             kubernetes.io/aws-ebs   Delete
```

The important setting is:

```yaml
parameters:
  type: gp3
```

