# 23. Create Internet-Facing ALB for Kibana

For production, HTTPS is recommended.

The following configuration creates:

```text
Internet
   |
   | HTTP :80
   v
ALB
   |
   | HTTPS :5601
   v
Kibana
```

However, Kibana requires a secure connection for login. Therefore, the recommended configuration is:

```text
Internet
   |
   | HTTP :80
   v
ALB
   |
   | redirect
   v
HTTPS :443
   |
   | HTTPS :5601
   v
Kibana
```

---

# 24. HTTPS ALB Requirements

You need:

* A DNS name
* ACM certificate
* Certificate ARN
* DNS record pointing to the ALB

Example:

```text
kibana.example.com
```

The ACM certificate should cover:

```text
kibana.example.com
```

---

# 25. Kibana ALB Ingress

Create:

```bash
vi kibana-alb.yaml
```

Use:

```yaml
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress

metadata:
  name: kibana-alb
  namespace: elastic

  annotations:

    # Internet-facing ALB
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/scheme: internet-facing

    # Route directly to pod IPs
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/target-type: ip

    # HTTP and HTTPS listeners
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/listen-ports: '[{"HTTP":80},{"HTTPS":443}]'

    # Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/ssl-redirect: "443"

    # ACM certificate
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/certificate-arn: <ACM_CERTIFICATE_ARN>

    # ALB -> Kibana
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/backend-protocol: HTTPS

    # Health check
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/healthcheck-protocol: HTTPS
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/healthcheck-port: "5601"
    alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/healthcheck-path: /login

spec:

  ingressClassName: alb

  rules:

    - host: kibana.example.com

      http:

        paths:

          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix

            backend:

              service:
                name: kibana-kb-http
                port:
                  number: 5601
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply -f kibana-alb.yaml
```

